# What tools/package-toolchain.ps1 leaves out of the static Qt
# (F:/ct/qt-custom-6.11p8/6.11.3-yap, 8.2 GB, 6937 files).
#
#   drop <glob>   not packed at all
#   stub <path>   packed as an empty file
#
# Stubs are the Release libraries and objects a clean build.ps1 never reads
# (measured 2026-11-09: every file's last-access time set to 2001, a clean
# build into an empty build dir, then the .lib/.obj files still at 2001).
# They stay as empty files because CMake's imported targets check that
# each library of a loaded Qt package exists, even one nothing links; a
# build that does link one fails at the link with a corrupt-file error.
# Among them: the QML tooling plugins (YAP_QML_PROFILER=ON needs the full
# Qt), QmlDom/QmlCompiler (used only inside the host tools, which are
# self-contained exes), the test libraries, the Labs modules, SpatialAudio
# and the unused platform and image plugins.
#
# Everything else is packed, read or not (headers, cmake files, mkspecs,
# qml type files and host tools: 188 MB of unread files, kept so a
# different build path does not trip over a missing one).
#
# To measure again after a Qt or CMakeLists.txt change: set LastAccessTime
# of every file under the Qt prefix to 2001-01-01, run build.ps1 into a new
# build dir, and list the .lib/.obj files whose LastAccessTime did not move
# (NTFS updates it on the first read when it is over an hour old). Do not
# read the Qt folder in between (grep, antivirus scans of it, copies).

drop doc/**
drop sbom/**
drop bin/*.pdb

